## 📊 Rigorous Verification & Health Checks

To verify compliance with the capstone criteria, the following test script checks every service interface directly via terminal calls:

```bash
# 1. Inspect Vault Key Allocation
VAULT_TOKEN=$(cat /root/code/vault-token)
curl -s -H "X-Vault-Token: $VAULT_TOKEN" http://localhost:8200/v1/secret/data/mlflow \
  | python3 -c "import json, sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin)['data']['data']; print('Vault Status -> Keys Staged:', list(d.keys()))"

# 2. Inspect Pull Request Status Configuration
GITEA_TOKEN=$(cat /root/.gitea/token)
curl -s -H "Authorization: token $GITEA_TOKEN" 'http://localhost:3000/api/v1/repos/gitea-admin/fraud-detector/pulls?state=all' \
  | python3 -c "
import json, sys
pr = next(p for p in json.load(sys.stdin) if p['head']['ref']=='production-release')
print('Gitea Status -> PR Merged:', pr['merged'])
print('Gitea Status -> Target Commit SHA:', pr['head']['sha'][:8])
"

# 3. Inspect MLflow Alias Target Registration
curl -s 'http://localhost:5000/api/2.0/mlflow/registered-models/alias?name=fraud-detector&alias=production' \
  | python3 -c "import json, sys; obj=json.load(sys.stdin)['model_version']; print(f'MLflow Status -> Model: {obj[\"name\"]}, Active Version: {obj[\"version\"]}, Alias Target: {obj[\"aliases\"]}')"
```

